;; The files of the checker's check (bin/ci annotations; doc/C23-SURVEY.md, "As built: C4") that do not pass and
;; that no automatic class explains (cc's gaps by the items' features, the pp-known and gcc-rejects files), by corpus,
;; each with its class (the classes below). Written by bin/ci annotations --record, the classes kept. Read with the
;; Clojure reader.
{:classes
 {:cc-attr-mode "GNU's mode attribute, which cc ignores (the checker gives gcc's type of that width)"
  :cc-c23-constants "C23's nullptr, true and false: cc's Builtin macros ((void*)0, 1, 0) where the checker types nullptr_t and bool"
  :cc-empty-init "an array of unknown size with an empty initializer {}: gcc 15.2's zero-length array, cc's incomplete one"
  :cc-layout "cc's layout of a struct or union differs from the checker's and gcc 15.2 agrees with the checker (asked by static assertions of the checker's sizes, alignments and offsets appended to the file: .tmp/c4/layout_judge.py, C4.3): packed, aligned and bit-field placements cc's abi.go does not follow"
  :cc-preprocessor "the file's stream differs from cc's: C23's #elifdef and __has_c_attribute, which cc's preprocessor lacks (test/c/c23/, which the token check does not cover)"
  :cc-redeclared "cc writes a redeclared array's or function's later (composite) type at the earlier declarator"
  :checker-gap "a difference neither cc's known gaps nor the reference explain: the checker's to look at (CS93)"
  :checker-layout "the checker's layout differs from cc's and gcc 15.2's static assertions refuse the checker's values: the checker's to fix (CS93)"
  :converter-gap "the forms lose what the checker needs: an imaginary constant's f suffix ((imaginary x) for xif), CS83 (a)'s class"
  :enum-range "an enumerator beyond long long's range in an error test (gcc rejects the value; cc wraps it, the checker does not)"
  :item-placement "an item cc places on another line or file than the forms (a #line directive, a table brought in by an #include among the items)"
  :layout-unjudged "a layout cc and the checker part on that the one-off judge could not ask gcc about (an anonymous or block-scope record, or the file not compiling with the assertions)"
  :vector-types "GNU's vector types, read and checked, out of eval and AOT by design (doc/c/SPEC.md §14); cc reads them as their elements"}
 :annot
